    "created_at": "2020-02-14T15:26:37Z",
    "updated_at": "2020-05-07T12:34:52Z",
    "body": "In that case we should act as if it had target=_blank right? (Including the recent addition of rel=noopener defaulting.) As those schemes open some other application. Though leaving that up to the user agent seems fine, as long as the top-level browsing context gets replaced so there's no connection between the two sites.\r\n\r\nAnyway, I'm very much supportive of the overall idea here. My take thus far was blocking non-top-level navigations, but this would work too. (Except this would not work when setting `location` directly, so we probably need both.)\r\n\r\nSomewhat related: #198 and #3043.",
